# <%= current_page.data.title %>

As well as the [VPC endpoints provided in each VPC](networking-approach.html#protected), the Modernisation Platform runs a **centralised VPC endpoints hub** in the core network services account.

This is a dedicated VPC containing [interface endpoints](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints.html) for a wide range of AWS services, shared across the whole platform.

## Why we do this

Interface endpoints are charged per endpoint, per availability zone, per hour. Creating an endpoint for every service in every business unit VPC would be expensive and would consume a lot of address space in the protected subnets.

By running one set of endpoints centrally and routing to them over the [Transit Gateway](networking-approach.html#transit-gateway), we can offer many more services than would otherwise be practical.

## How traffic reaches it

The hub VPC is attached to the Transit Gateway with its own route table. Both live data and non-live data VPC attachments are propagated into that route table, and a static route for the hub VPC CIDR is added to the `live_data` and `non_live_data` route tables.

This means resources in your VPC can reach the centralised endpoints, and return traffic can find its way back, without any configuration on your part.

The hub VPC uses the range `10.20.240.0/20`, as recorded in the [CIDR allocation register](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform/blob/main/cidr-allocation.md).

## Available services

The current list is maintained in [centralised-vpc-endpoints.json](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform/blob/main/terraform/environments/core-network-services/centralised-vpc-endpoints.json). At the time of writing it covers:

`apigateway`, `athena`, `backup`, `cloudtrail`, `config`, `detective`, `dms`, `ec2`, `ec2messages`, `ecr.api`, `ecr.dkr`, `eks`, `eks-auth`, `elasticache`, `email`, `email-smtp`, `events`, `guardduty-data`, `inspector2`, `kinesis-firehose`, `kms`, `lambda`, `logs`, `rds`, `rds-data`, `secretsmanager`, `securityhub`, `sns`, `sqs`, `ssm`, `ssmmessages`, `sts`, `transcribe`, `wafv2`

Please check the JSON file for the current list rather than relying on this page.

## Relationship to per-VPC endpoints

A small number of endpoints are still created in each VPC's protected subnets, because they are needed for core functionality such as [Systems Manager Session Manager](instance-access-and-bastions.html) access. These are EC2, EC2 Messages, SSM and SSM Messages, plus a gateway endpoint for S3.

Everything else should be reached through the centralised hub.

If you need a service that is not currently available, please ask in [#ask-modernisation-platform](https://mojdt.slack.com/archives/C01A7QK5VM1).
